window.RB_INDEX = [{"page": "index.html", "chapter": "Start here", "section": "What is RemBase?", "anchor": "what-is-rembase", "text": "RemBase is our new inventory system. It will replace Fishbowl on December 1, 2026 . RemBase has pages for stock, purchase orders, receiving, counting, production runs and Amazon shipments."}, {"page": "index.html", "chapter": "Start here", "section": "Until December 1: Fishbowl is real, RemBase is practice", "anchor": "until-december-1-fishbowl-is-real-rembase-is-practice", "text": "Do all real work in Fishbowl. Use RemBase only to practice. RemBase is copied from Fishbowl every night. The nightly copy does not touch TEST items, so your TEST practice stays. Practice on a real part is reset by the nightly copy. That is one more reason to practice only on TEST items. If you are not sure where to do something, do it in Fishbowl. Then ask the person for that area (see Who to ask )."}, {"page": "index.html", "chapter": "Start here", "section": "Practice only with TEST items", "anchor": "practice-only-with-test-items", "text": "Each person has their own practice PO, parts and practice run: Person Receive this PO Your parts (scan code) Build this run Count this bin Becca TEST-PRACTICE-BECCA-2 TEST-BECCA-A (#9111#), TEST-BECCA-B (#9112#) TEST-PRACTICE-RUN-BECCA TEST-BIN (#9001#) Chad TEST-PRACTICE-CHAD-2 TEST-CHAD-A (#9121#), TEST-CHAD-B (#9122#) TEST-PRACTICE-RUN-CHAD TEST-BIN (#9001#) Sabith TEST-PRACTICE-SABITH-2 TEST-SABITH-A (#9131#), TEST-SABITH-B (#9132#) TEST-PRACTICE-RUN-SABITH TEST-BIN (#9001#) Your parts start at 0. Receive them into TEST-BIN . Your first practice PO (TEST-PRACTICE-BECCA, -CHAD or -SABITH) m"}, {"page": "index.html", "chapter": "Start here", "section": "How to open RemBase", "anchor": "how-to-open-rembase", "text": "Open the RemBase link that Becca sent you. Sign in with your work Airtable account. You see the menu on the left side. The RemBase menu on the left side of the screen"}, {"page": "index.html", "chapter": "Start here", "section": "The menu", "anchor": "the-menu", "text": "Page What it is for Home Reports, today’s sales, Amazon storage space, aged stock, listing alerts and other summaries. See Home . Inventory Find a part. See how much we have and where. Cycle Count Count the stock in a bin. Purchase Orders Make and track orders to vendors. Receiving See what is arriving from vendors. Run Planning Decide what to build next. Production Run Build kits and packs. Enter what you built. FBA Shipment Send stock to Amazon. Print box labels. Approvals Big stock changes that need a “yes” first. Flags Problems the system found. Returns Grading Check items that Amazon sent"}, {"page": "index.html", "chapter": "Start here", "section": "The most important rules", "anchor": "the-most-important-rules", "text": "Real work goes in Fishbowl until December 1. Practice only with TEST items. Some buttons send money, emails or orders. Read Do not press before you start. Not sure? Stop and ask. See Who to ask ."}, {"page": "index.html", "chapter": "Start here", "section": "About the pictures", "anchor": "about-the-pictures", "text": "Every picture comes from RemBase. A red box shows what to click or type. A red number is the step number. A red ✕ means do not press . An orange box means a real button : you may press it, but be careful. An orange $ means the button costs money . Black boxes hide private data such as prices, vendors, customers and Amazon numbers. You see the real data in RemBase."}, {"page": "becca-try-it.html", "chapter": "\"Becca: try it\"", "section": "Read this first", "anchor": "read-this-first", "text": "Until December 1, real work stays in Fishbowl. In RemBase you only look, or you practice on TEST items. Your practice items: first PO TEST-PRACTICE-BECCA (finish it in Task 4), new PO TEST-PRACTICE-BECCA-2 with your parts TEST-BECCA-A (#9111#) and TEST-BECCA-B (#9112#), bin TEST-BIN (#9001#). RemBase saves by itself. There is no Save button. Press Tab or click outside the box. Never delete anything. If something gets deleted by mistake, tell Adam. Nothing else is needed. Made a typing mistake? Press Cmd+Z ( Ctrl+Z on Windows) right away to undo it. While you practice, never press these buttons"}, {"page": "becca-try-it.html", "chapter": "\"Becca: try it\"", "section": "Task 1 – Morning check on Home (look only)", "anchor": "task-1-morning-check-on-home-look-only", "text": "Goal: see today’s sales, our Amazon storage space and our aged stock in one place. In the RemBase menu, click Home , then Home . Sign in with your work Airtable account if it asks. Look at the first box, Today so far . This is today’s Amazon sales, so far. It updates every hour. It is not the full day. D – Note says how much is an estimate. Scroll down to Sales (Amazon.com) . Look at Last full day sales . This is yesterday’s final number. Scroll down to FBA storage space . Look at E – Level . OK (green) = fine. Watch (yellow) = 85% of our limit or more. Over (red) = 100% of our limit or more. "}, {"page": "becca-try-it.html", "chapter": "\"Becca: try it\"", "section": "Task 2 – Open the Inventory Pipeline file (look only)", "anchor": "task-2-open-the-inventory-pipeline-file-look-only", "text": "Goal: open the newest Inventory Pipeline file for ordering and send-in planning. In the RemBase menu, click Home , then Reports . At the top, look at the two counters: A – Reports late or stale and B – Library not refreshed (36 h) . Both should be 0 . If one is not 0, look at the list Late or stale now under them and tell Adam which report. Find the list Newest file of each report . Click All brands to open that group. Find the row Inventory Pipeline . C – Status should say OK . Make sure you are signed in to Google with your work account. Click Drive Link on the Inventory Pipeline row. The fi"}, {"page": "becca-try-it.html", "chapter": "\"Becca: try it\"", "section": "Task 3 – Check listing alerts (look only)", "anchor": "task-3-check-listing-alerts-look-only", "text": "Goal: see which listings need you today. In the RemBase menu, click Home , then Listings . Look at the four counters: G – Open P1 (urgent) H – Open P2 I – Not buyable / status problems J – Buy box problems The numbers change every day. Look at the list Open P1 alerts (oldest first) . These are the urgent ones. P1 = it sells 10 or more a month, and it is out of stock, not active, or the buy box is suppressed while it has stock. For our own brands, also when we lost the buy box. The Brand column shows the brand of each row. The chart Open alerts by brand shows how many each brand has. For each r"}, {"page": "becca-try-it.html", "chapter": "\"Becca: try it\"", "section": "Task 4 – Practice: finish your first PO, then receive your new PO (TEST only)", "anchor": "task-4-practice-finish-your-first-po-then-receive-your-new-po-test-only", "text": "Goal: finish your first practice PO, then receive your new one. Always pick the bin. If a receipt has no bin, nothing is added to stock, and a flag appears within about an hour. Already saved a receipt with no bin? Do not receive again. Open the receipt: Receiving → your PO line → Received so far → click the receipt with no bin. In the box Add the bin (receipt not posted yet) , type or scan the bin barcode and press Enter . For practice, TEST-BIN’s barcode is #9001# . It posts once. Pick the line by product name ( TEST component A or TEST component B ), not by number. If a line already says Fu"}, {"page": "becca-try-it.html", "chapter": "\"Becca: try it\"", "section": "Task 5 – Practice: close a TEST flag (TEST only)", "anchor": "task-5-practice-close-a-test-flag-test-only", "text": "Goal: read a flag and mark it done. In the RemBase menu, click Flags , then All Open Flags . Do not use My Open Flags . It looks empty, because flags are not assigned to people yet. Search TEST-PRACTICE-BECCA . Click the flag Receipt reversed: TEST-PRACTICE-BECCA-L2 . Read the title and the Note . The note says to receive the line again with the right numbers. You did that in Task 4. Set Status to Resolved . The flag leaves the open list. If Task 4 made any new flag with TEST in the title, open it, read it and set it to Resolved too. Do not tick Escalate To Asana . It makes a real Asana task. "}, {"page": "becca-try-it.html", "chapter": "\"Becca: try it\"", "section": "Task 6 – Practice: add a line to a PO and open the PO PDF (TEST only)", "anchor": "task-6-practice-add-a-line-to-a-po-and-open-the-po-pdf-test-only", "text": "Goal: add one line to your new practice PO (TEST-PRACTICE-BECCA-2) and see the PDF update. In the RemBase menu, click Purchase Orders . Search TEST-PRACTICE-BECCA-2 and click the PO number. Only open PO numbers that start with TEST- or PRACTICE- . Real POs look like 2026-061. In PO Lines , click the + under the last line. A new empty line appears. Click the + in the new line’s Part cell. Type TEST-BECCA-A and click it in the list. Never click Create “…” at the bottom of the list. Point at the new line and click the expand button (two small arrows). Expand button to open a PO line Qty Ordered: "}, {"page": "becca-try-it.html", "chapter": "\"Becca: try it\"", "section": "Not in these steps (and why)", "anchor": "not-in-these-steps-and-why", "text": "PO Planning, Run Planning, New Part: the ticks are shared with real planning, and there is nothing safe to practice before December 1. You can look at them. Cycle count, production runs, Next shipment: floor jobs (Chad and Sabith). Claims: Karly’s weekly task. Ads: on hold."}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "What this chapter is for", "anchor": "what-this-chapter-is-for", "text": "Every page in RemBase works the same way. Learn these few things once."}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "Pick a page", "anchor": "pick-a-page", "text": "Click a page name in the menu on the left. Some pages have smaller pages under them. Click the smaller page you need. The RemBase menu"}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "Find something in a list", "anchor": "find-something-in-a-list", "text": "Most pages show a list. The buttons at the top right help you find things. Filter, Sort and Search buttons at the top right of a list Click the magnifying glass (Search). Type a part number, a name or a PO number. The list now shows only matching rows. To see everything again, click the ✕ in the search box. Filter hides rows you do not need. It changes only your own view. Sort changes the order of the rows. It changes only your own view."}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "Open a record", "anchor": "open-a-record", "text": "Click a row in the list. In some lists, point at the row and click the expand button (two small arrows). The record opens on the right side or in the middle. On the Home pages (Home, Listings, Reports), you can also click a number tile . It opens the list of records behind the number, and each of those opens too. Most record pages are read-only. Where you can write something, the page shows a box for it (for example Your check or Your plan )."}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "Move between records and close", "anchor": "move-between-records-and-close", "text": "Arrows and close button at the top of an open record A – the arrows go to the previous or next record in the list. B – the ✕ closes the record."}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "White boxes and grey text", "anchor": "white-boxes-and-grey-text", "text": "A white box with a border is a field you can type in. Grey text or text with no box is read-only. The system fills it in. RemBase saves what you type by itself. There is no Save button. Click outside the box or press Tab when you finish."}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "Undo, history and comments", "anchor": "undo-history-and-comments", "text": "Made a mistake while typing? Press Cmd+Z ( Ctrl+Z on Windows) right away to undo it. Stock changes are always recorded in the Ledger : who entered them and when (receipts, counts, builds, reversals, shipments). On a PO line, Price/Qty changed by / at shows who last changed the price or quantity. For anything else, ask Adam. He can see the full history. Comments on a record are visible to everyone."}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "How to scan", "anchor": "how-to-scan", "text": "RemBase Scan is a page for your phone. It shows what RemBase knows about an item or a bin. Ask Adam for the RemBase Scan bookmark. You sign in with your work Google account. Open the RemBase Scan bookmark. Scan a code in one of three ways: Pull the trigger on the Bluetooth scanner. You do not need to tap anything first. Tap the box and type the code. (TEST-BIN’s code is #9001# .) Tap Scan with camera . Read the result: An item shows its bins and how many are in each, its lots and expiration dates, and its open POs. A date in red expires in less than 90 days. A bin shows what is in it. Use the "}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Typing in the wrong record. Check the title at the top before you type. Typing on a real part. Before December 1, type only on TEST items. Thinking a filter is gone. A number next to Filter or Sort means one is on. Click it to remove it."}, {"page": "inventory.html", "chapter": "Inventory", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "Inventory shows every part. You can see how many we have in the warehouse and at Amazon, and in which bins. Who uses it: everyone looks here. Only Becca and Adam add new parts. For most people this page only shows information. You can look at real parts here. Do not change anything on a real part."}, {"page": "inventory.html", "chapter": "Inventory", "section": "The list", "anchor": "the-list", "text": "Inventory list with stock columns A – Warehouse On Hand Qty: how many are in our warehouse. B – FBA On Hand Qty: how many are at Amazon. Stock moving between Amazon warehouses counts as stock at Amazon. Some parts have more than one Amazon SKU, for example a “-stickered” SKU and the original. RemBase adds them up. Each Amazon label (FNSKU) is counted once. FBA Inbound Qty is added up the same way. Every night RemBase checks Amazon’s report. If a part is missing from two daily reports in a row, RemBase sets FBA On Hand Qty and FBA Inbound Qty to 0 and leaves Days Of Cover FBA blank. If a night’"}, {"page": "inventory.html", "chapter": "Inventory", "section": "Task: find a part and see its stock", "anchor": "task-find-a-part-and-see-its-stock", "text": "Click Inventory in the menu. Click the magnifying glass at the top right. Search button on the Inventory list Type the part number. For practice, type TEST-COMP-A . Search box with a part number typed in Click the part in the list. One search result: the practice part The part page opens. At the top you see the stock numbers. Top of the part page with stock numbers Scroll down. You see more sections: Lots, bin summary and ledger sections of a part 5 – Lots: each lot, its expiration date, its bin and how many are left. 6 – Part x Bin Summary: how many are in each bin. It updates every hour. 7 –"}, {"page": "inventory.html", "chapter": "Inventory", "section": "What you should see", "anchor": "what-you-should-see", "text": "For a TEST part after a practice receipt: Warehouse On Hand Qty went up by what you received. A lot with your expiration date in TEST-BIN . A ledger line of type Receipt for your receipt. The numbers may differ from what you expect: others practice on the shared TEST parts too. Your own parts (for example TEST-BECCA-A) start at 0."}, {"page": "inventory.html", "chapter": "Inventory", "section": "Task: add a new part (Becca and Adam only)", "anchor": "task-add-a-new-part-becca-and-adam-only", "text": "Only Becca and Adam add new parts. Everyone else: ask Becca to add the part. Click Inventory in the menu. Click New Part at the top right. New Part button at the top right of the Inventory page A form opens. Type the SKU (A). You must fill it in. Top of the New Part form with the SKU box marked Fill in the other boxes you know. Scroll down. Created via form (B) is ticked by itself. You cannot untick it. Click Create (C). Bottom of the New Part form with Created via form ticked and the Create button Always use New Part. A part made any other way (the data grid, an import, or Create “…” in a par"}, {"page": "inventory.html", "chapter": "Inventory", "section": "Words on this page", "anchor": "words-on-this-page", "text": "Where (bins) shows the bins that hold this part. Scan Keys are the codes you can scan to find this part (for example the UPC and the Amazon label). Amazon ASIN is the ASIN of the part’s active Amazon listing. If a part has two active Amazon SKUs, the Ship as SKU’s ASIN comes first. Blank means RemBase has no active ASIN for the part yet. You can still search by ASIN. Max Available to Build is not stock. For a pack, it is how many packs the parts can make. For a single part that goes into packs, it is what is left after the packs take their share. See Run Planning . Open PO Qty is how many are "}, {"page": "inventory.html", "chapter": "Inventory", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Reading the wrong column. Warehouse and Amazon (FBA) are two different numbers. Expecting Part x Bin Summary right away. It can take up to one hour to update. Making a part another way. Only use New Part . A part made from a part list ( Create “…” ) is left out of planning. Pressing New Part if you are not Becca or Adam. Ask Becca to add the part."}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "A purchase order (PO) is an order we send to a vendor. Each PO has lines . One line = one part and how many we ordered. Who uses it: Becca makes and sends POs. Everyone can look. Before December 1, make real POs in Fishbowl . In RemBase, practice only on your own practice PO (TEST-PRACTICE-BECCA-2, -CHAD-2 or -SABITH-2). A brand-new PO you make before December 1 gets a PRACTICE- number, not a real PO number. Use the TEST Vendor and TEST parts on it. The pictures use TEST-HB-1."}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "Sub-pages", "anchor": "sub-pages", "text": "Sub-page What it is for Purchase Orders All POs. Open one to see its lines. PO Planning What we should order next. PO Planning – Commit Turns the planning ticks into POs. Becca only. PO Variance Report PO lines that came in short, over or damaged. Excluded from planning Parts that planning ignores, like TEST parts."}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "Task: find and open a PO", "anchor": "task-find-and-open-a-po", "text": "Click Purchase Orders in the menu. Find the PO in the list. For practice, use your own practice PO . Click the PO number. Purchase order list with the practice PO at the top The PO opens on the right. You see its status, vendor, dates, notes and lines. PO status: Issued – the PO is placed. Nothing has arrived yet. Partial – some of it has arrived. Fulfilled – everything has arrived. Closed Short – closed before everything arrived. Cancelled – the PO was made by mistake or is not needed. To stop a PO, set Status to Cancelled . Never delete a PO. (There is no Delete button for POs or PO lines.)"}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "Task: add a line to a PO (practice)", "anchor": "task-add-a-line-to-a-po-practice", "text": "Open your own practice PO . Add a line for one of your own parts (for example TEST-BECCA-A). In PO Lines , click the + under the last line. Practice PO page with the add-line plus sign A new line appears. Click the + in its Part cell. Plus button inside the Part cell of a new line Type the part number. Click the right part in the list. Part picker showing the practice parts Never click Create “…” at the bottom of this list. It makes a new part that is left out of planning, and Becca gets a flag. If the part is missing, ask Becca to add it. Point at the new line. Click the expand button (two sm"}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "PO status and Order Date", "anchor": "po-status-and-order-date", "text": "RemBase fills these in by itself: A new PO gets Status = Issued and today’s Order Date . When stock is received, the status changes to Partial or Fulfilled by itself. You only change the status by hand if Becca asks you to. Click the Status box and choose the status. Status list with Issued"}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "PO numbers", "anchor": "po-numbers", "text": "A PO number starts with the year. Each new year starts again at 001. Before December 1, every new PO gets a PRACTICE- number. This is true for a PO you make on the Purchase Orders page and for a PO that PO Planning makes. Before December 1, PO Planning does not add lines to a real PO."}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "What you should see", "anchor": "what-you-should-see", "text": "Finished practice PO with two lines Status Issued . When the stock arrives, it changes to Partial or Fulfilled by itself. (TEST-HB-1 is now Fulfilled , because both lines were received.) The lines are listed under PO Lines . Total Outstanding Qty = what has not arrived yet. Issued Warning: if a PO was already sent to the vendor, a change here does not reach the vendor. Tell the vendor yourself. Price/Qty changed by and Price/Qty changed at (on a PO line): who last changed the price or the quantity on this line, and when. Automations means the system filled it (for example the last-paid price, "}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "To print a PO", "anchor": "to-print-a-po", "text": "Open the PO. Click the file under PO PDF . Print it from your browser. RemBase makes the PDF by itself and makes it again after every change. Do not upload or change it by hand. If the file is missing after a few minutes, ask Adam."}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "PO Planning (look only)", "anchor": "po-planning-look-only", "text": "PO Planning shows what we should order. PO Planning list 1 – Recommended Order Qty: how many the system suggests we order. It covers the next 90 days of sales. It uses the last 30 days’ sales rate. It is adjusted for the season (more before the holidays). Stock moving between Amazon warehouses counts as stock at Amazon. Clear Conscience lens and liquid show 0 . Consigned stock that we can buy any time covers them. PO Planning columns and the Commit button 2 – Planning Override Qty: Becca types her own number here. 3 – Start New PO: tick to start a new PO for this part. 4 – Planning Add To PO: "}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "PO Planning – Commit (Becca only)", "anchor": "po-planning-commit-becca-only", "text": "Commit page with its two buttons marked do not press Commit PO Planning makes the POs from the ticked rows. Clear PO Planning Selections removes all the ticks. Before December 1, Commit only makes PRACTICE- POs. It does not add lines to a real PO. Do not press these unless you are Becca."}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "Excluded from planning", "anchor": "excluded-from-planning", "text": "Parts excluded from planning These parts are left out of planning. To bring a part back, Becca unticks Exclude from planning ."}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Pressing Email PO. It emails the vendor. See Do not press . Clicking Create “…” in the part list. It makes a new part that planning leaves out. Ask Becca to add the part. Changing an Issued PO and not telling the vendor. RemBase does not tell them. Ticking boxes in PO Planning to “try it”. The ticks are shared with Becca’s real planning."}, {"page": "receiving.html", "chapter": "Receiving", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "When boxes arrive from a vendor, you receive them. Receiving puts the stock in a bin with its expiration date. Who uses it: Chad and Sabith. Before December 1, receive real deliveries in Fishbowl . In RemBase, practice only on your own practice PO (TEST-PRACTICE-BECCA-2, -CHAD-2 or -SABITH-2). The pictures use TEST-HB-1."}, {"page": "receiving.html", "chapter": "Receiving", "section": "The Receiving page", "anchor": "the-receiving-page", "text": "Receiving list with the practice lines Click Receiving in the menu (1). Use Search (2) to find a PO number or a part. Each row is one PO line that still has something to receive. Click a row to see what was ordered and what has arrived. When everything on a line has arrived, the line leaves this list. Each row also shows the product’s scan keys (the codes you can scan). On the line page, Cost from last paid. Check it. means the Unit Cost was filled in from the last price paid. Price/Qty changed by / at shows who last changed the price or quantity, and when. See Purchase Orders . During practic"}, {"page": "receiving.html", "chapter": "Receiving", "section": "Task: receive a PO line", "anchor": "task-receive-a-po-line", "text": "There are three ways to open the Receive form. All three open the same form. Way 1 is the easiest. Way 1 – from the Receiving page Click Receiving in the menu. Click your line (for practice: your own practice PO ). Scroll down to Received so far . Click Receive (3). Receive button on the Receiving page Way 2 – from Purchase Orders Click Purchase Orders in the menu. Click the PO number. In PO Lines , point at the line. Click the small expand icon (⤢) at the left of the row. A plain click on the row only selects a box, it does not open the line. The expand icon at the left of a PO line Next to R"}, {"page": "receiving.html", "chapter": "Receiving", "section": "What you should see", "anchor": "what-you-should-see", "text": "The receipt appears under Received so far (and under Receipt Lines on the PO line): Quantities and the receipt list after receiving Qty Received goes up. Outstanding Qty goes down. Derived Status says Partial or Fulfilled . Received so far lists each receipt with the bin, the expiration date, who received it, and Received At : the date and time in Eastern time. The stock is now on the part page in Inventory ."}, {"page": "receiving.html", "chapter": "Receiving", "section": "Open POs", "anchor": "open-pos", "text": "Receiving → Open POs lists POs that are not finished, with how much is still outstanding. Click a PO to open it, then receive a line as in Way 2. Open POs list"}, {"page": "receiving.html", "chapter": "Receiving", "section": "Forgot the bin", "anchor": "forgot-the-bin", "text": "Already saved a receipt with no bin? Do not receive again. Open the receipt: Receiving → your PO line → Received so far → click the receipt with no bin. In the box Add the bin (receipt not posted yet) , type or scan the bin barcode and press Enter . For practice, TEST-BIN’s barcode is #9001# . The receipt posts once."}, {"page": "receiving.html", "chapter": "Receiving", "section": "Fix a wrong receipt", "anchor": "fix-a-wrong-receipt", "text": "Anyone may press Reverse this receipt . Open the receipt: Receiving → the PO line → Received so far → click the receipt. Press Reverse this receipt . Read Reverse Result . OK means the stock was taken back out, the receipt is marked Reversed , and a flag was made. Receive the line again with the right numbers. A new receipt is made (…-R2). If Reverse Result says: Message What it means REFUSED … Ask a manager The stock was already used or moved. Nothing changed. Tell Becca or Chad. REFUSED: this receipt was never posted to stock Nothing to reverse. Use Add the bin instead. REFUSED … came from F"}, {"page": "receiving.html", "chapter": "Receiving", "section": "Wrong amounts on a PO", "anchor": "wrong-amounts-on-a-po", "text": "PO line with Line Type and the Close this line short box marked Something arrived that is not on the PO (Not Ordered) Before December 1, Becca first adds the line in Fishbowl , with the price from the vendor. Then it is received as normal. In RemBase the line shows A – Line Type: Not Ordered . Never receive it on the line of another product. More arrived than we ordered (Over) Receive what arrived. RemBase makes a flag for Becca about the extra units. If the extra units cost nothing, no approval is needed. Less arrived than we ordered (Short) The rest is still coming: leave the line open. The "}, {"page": "receiving.html", "chapter": "Receiving", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Typing cases in the Units box. Units = single items. Cases = full cases. No expiration date. Without a date the system cannot use the oldest stock first. Wrong bin. Choose the bin where the stock really is. Receiving an item on the wrong line. If it is not on the PO, ask Becca to add a Not Ordered line first. No bin, or a bin scan that does not match one bin. The receipt is not posted, and a flag appears within about an hour. Do not receive again. Add the bin . Then it posts once. Receiving twice. Look at Received so far before you receive. Saving a receipt with no quantity. RemBase raises a f"}, {"page": "cycle-count.html", "chapter": "Cycle Count", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "A cycle count means you count what is really in one bin and compare it with RemBase. Who uses it: Chad and Sabith. Before December 1, do real counts in Fishbowl . In RemBase, practice only on TEST-BIN . If you complete a count session on a real bin before December 1, RemBase changes no stock. It makes one flag (“Practice count…”). A count session with status Failed – floor app or Cancelled – duplicate : never complete it. Count the bin again. In the Cycle Count list, each bin shows its scan code and what is in it. You can also scan a bin with RemBase Scan . See Basics ."}, {"page": "cycle-count.html", "chapter": "Cycle Count", "section": "Sub-pages", "anchor": "sub-pages", "text": "Sub-page What it is for Cycle Count All bins. Open a bin to count it. Count by Part All parts with their warehouse stock. Read-only."}, {"page": "cycle-count.html", "chapter": "Cycle Count", "section": "Task: start a count", "anchor": "task-start-a-count", "text": "Click Cycle Count in the menu. Type the bin name in Search (1). For practice: TEST-BIN . Click the bin in the list. Scroll down to Count Sessions . Click Start Count Session (2). Bin page with the Start Count Session button A form opens. Counted By shows your name (A). Click Create (3). Start count form The new session appears under Count Sessions . Click it."}, {"page": "cycle-count.html", "chapter": "Cycle Count", "section": "Task: enter your count", "anchor": "task-enter-your-count", "text": "RemBase makes one count line (4) for each part and lot in the bin. Expected is what RemBase thinks is there. Count session with its count lines Open the session. Click each line under Count Lines . Count that part in the bin. Type the number you counted in Actual Qty (6). Expected Qty (A) shows what RemBase thinks is there. A count line with Expected Qty and Actual Qty Close the line (✕ at the top right). Do the same for every line. When every line has a number, click Status and choose Completed (7). Status list with Completed Count every line. If you leave a line empty, RemBase skips it and c"}, {"page": "cycle-count.html", "chapter": "Cycle Count", "section": "What you should see", "anchor": "what-you-should-see", "text": "Finished count session The session status is Completed , with the time it was completed. The bin shows a new Last Counted Date . If your count was different, RemBase makes a Flag for Becca and changes the stock: a small difference (under the approval limit) changes the stock right away; a big difference waits in Approvals until Becca or Adam says yes."}, {"page": "cycle-count.html", "chapter": "Cycle Count", "section": "Count by Part", "anchor": "count-by-part", "text": "Count by Part list This list shows each part and its warehouse stock. Use it to check a number. It is read-only."}, {"page": "cycle-count.html", "chapter": "Cycle Count", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Counting the wrong bin. Check the bin name at the top before you count. Leaving a line empty. RemBase skips it, so that part is not counted. Counting cases instead of units. Count single units. Starting two sessions for one bin. Look at Count Sessions first."}, {"page": "run-planning.html", "chapter": "Run Planning", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "Run Planning shows which products we should build and send to Amazon next. Who uses it: Becca and Adam decide. Chad can read it to see what is coming."}, {"page": "run-planning.html", "chapter": "Run Planning", "section": "The list", "anchor": "the-list", "text": "Run Planning list and its main columns 1 – Recommended Send Qty: how many the system suggests we build and send. It plans enough stock at Amazon for 45 days , plus the days Amazon needs to receive a shipment (about 12 days now; RemBase updates this every day). The list is sorted by this number. 2 – Run Planning Override Qty: Becca types her own number here to replace the suggestion. 3 – Run Planning Add To Run: tick to put this product in the next runs. 4 – Max Available to Build: how many we could build with the parts we have now. Days Of Cover FBA: how many days the stock at Amazon will last"}, {"page": "run-planning.html", "chapter": "Run Planning", "section": "Run Planning – Commit (Becca only)", "anchor": "run-planning-commit-becca-only", "text": "Run Planning commit page with buttons marked do not press Commit Run Planning makes production runs from the ticked rows. Clear Run Planning removes all the ticks. Planned runs lists the runs it made. Do not press these unless you are Becca."}, {"page": "run-planning.html", "chapter": "Run Planning", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Reading Max Available to Build as stock. It is not stock. Ticking Add To Run to “try it”. The ticks are shared. Becca’s next commit would use them. Thinking a number is wrong during the hourly update. Wait a few minutes."}, {"page": "production-run.html", "chapter": "Production Run", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "A production run is one job where we build a product from its parts. Example: a 2-pack is built from two single items. Who uses it: Chad and Sabith on the floor. Becca plans the runs. Before December 1, enter real runs in Fishbowl . In RemBase, practice only on your own practice run (TEST-PRACTICE-RUN-BECCA, -CHAD or -SABITH). Never press Finish Run on a real run before December 1. You may press it on your own practice run."}, {"page": "production-run.html", "chapter": "Production Run", "section": "Sub-pages", "anchor": "sub-pages", "text": "Sub-page What it is for Production Run The office view: plan, components and lots. Production Run – Floor The floor view: what you built, cartons and pallet."}, {"page": "production-run.html", "chapter": "Production Run", "section": "Task: find a run and check its parts", "anchor": "task-find-a-run-and-check-its-parts", "text": "Click Production Run in the menu. Click the run in the list (1). The list is sorted by due date. Production run page for the practice run Check Qty Planned (2). This is how many to build. Check Output Part . This is the product you build. Run Cartons (3) will show the boxes after you enter them on the Floor page. Scroll down to Run Components (4). Components the run will use, with lots Component Part SKU: each part you need. Qty To Consume: how many of that part. Chosen Lot (5): which lot to take. RemBase picks the lot that expires first. If Run Components is empty, RemBase has no recipe for t"}, {"page": "production-run.html", "chapter": "Production Run", "section": "Task: enter what you built (Floor page)", "anchor": "task-enter-what-you-built-floor-page", "text": "Click Production Run – Floor in the menu. Click your run in the list. Floor page with Qty Built and cartons Type the number you built in Qty Built (6). In Run Cartons , click the + (7) to add a carton row. Fill in the row. Press Tab to go to the next box: Boxes: how many boxes of this size. Units Per Box: how many units in each box. Length , Width , Height: box size in inches. Weight Per Box (lb): weight of one full box in pounds. If you have boxes of different sizes, add one row per size. If you built fewer than planned, choose a Short-Close Reason and write a Short-Close Note ."}, {"page": "production-run.html", "chapter": "Production Run", "section": "What you should see", "anchor": "what-you-should-see", "text": "Floor page after typing the built quantity and cartons Qty Built shows your number. Run Stage changes to In Progress . Units in Run Cartons = Boxes × Units Per Box. It should match Qty Built. Missing is empty when the carton row is complete."}, {"page": "production-run.html", "chapter": "Production Run", "section": "Task: finish the run", "anchor": "task-finish-the-run", "text": "When the run is built and the cartons are entered, Finish Run takes the parts out of stock and adds the finished product. On a real run it also adds the units to the next Amazon shipment. Practice: you may press Finish Run on your own practice run . Your practice run is not linked to any Amazon shipment, and its Staging Pallet is TEST-BIN , so the finished TEST kits go to TEST-BIN. Do not change the Staging Pallet. Check Qty Built and the Run Cartons again. Click Finish Run at the top right. Press it once . Read Finish Result : DONE … – the run is finished. NOT DONE: … – nothing was changed. T"}, {"page": "production-run.html", "chapter": "Production Run", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Pressing Finish Run on a real run. Before December 1, only on your own practice run. Pressing Finish Run twice. Press once and read Finish Result . Units do not match Qty Built. Check Boxes × Units Per Box. Weight of the whole stack instead of one box. Type the weight of one box. Taking a different lot than Chosen Lot. Use the lot RemBase picked, or tell Chad."}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "FBA means Amazon stores and ships our products. We send boxes to Amazon warehouses. This page plans those shipments, gets the labels and tracks what Amazon received. Who uses it: anyone on the team. Chad usually prints the labels and packs the boxes. The buttons on this page are REAL, not practice. They talk to Amazon for a real shipment. Confirm placement and Confirm freight cost money. Check the price first. Press a button once . Then wait until Inbound Pending is empty again. Not sure? Ask Adam before you press."}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "Sub-pages", "anchor": "sub-pages", "text": "Sub-page What it is for Sent to Amazon Every shipment we sent, and how much Amazon received. Next shipment The shipment we are building now. Labels are here. Sent from this plan The lines that went out with the last plan."}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "Task: check a shipment we sent", "anchor": "task-check-a-shipment-we-sent", "text": "Click FBA Shipment in the menu. Click Sent to Amazon (1). Click a shipment in the list (2). List of shipments sent to Amazon, ids hidden Read the numbers: One shipment with its numbers Status: Shipped, Receiving, Closed or Cancelled. Total Units: how many we sent. Qty Received By Amazon (3): how many Amazon has counted. Qty Remaining: how many Amazon has not counted yet. FBA Shipment Lines (4): one line per product."}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "The Next shipment page", "anchor": "the-next-shipment-page", "text": "Next shipment page, ids, prices and labels hidden Read it from top to bottom: 1 – Inbound Pending: a button was pressed and RemBase is working on it. Wait. 2 – Inbound Result: the last message from RemBase. It tells you the next step. While Amazon is working it says what is happening, for example “Getting carrier quotes from Amazon. This takes a few minutes.” Wait until it changes. 3 – Label Files: the box labels, pallet labels and Bill of Lading (BOL). Ship Date , Freight Class: shipping details. Approved Placement Price , Approved Carrier Total: what Amazon and the carrier charge (hidden on "}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "Task: print the box labels", "anchor": "task-print-the-box-labels", "text": "Open FBA Shipment → Next shipment . Read Inbound Result . It says when the labels are ready. Under Label Files , click the file you need. The files come in two steps: After Confirm placement : the two box label files. After Confirm freight (truck / LTL shipments only): the pallet labels and the bill of lading . The files: box labels letter 6-up – six labels on one letter page. box labels 4x6 thermal – for the label printer. pallet labels – Amazon gives four labels for each pallet , one for each side. bill of lading – the paper for the truck driver. The file opens. Print it. Put one box label o"}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "Sent from this plan", "anchor": "sent-from-this-plan", "text": "FBA Shipment → Sent from this plan lists each product line that went out with the last plan: how many units, when, and which Amazon shipment it went in. It is read-only. Lines sent from the last plan, ids hidden"}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "The buttons, in order (real buttons: be careful)", "anchor": "the-buttons-in-order-real-buttons-be-careful", "text": "Anyone on the team may press these for a real shipment. They work on any open shipment that is not a TEST shipment. Read what each one does first. Button What it does Create plan Starts a new shipment plan with Amazon. Refresh options Asks Amazon again for warehouse choices. Confirm placement Accepts the Amazon warehouse choice. Costs money. Get prices again Asks carriers for new prices. Does not cost money. Confirm freight Books the carrier. Costs money. Re-check Asks Amazon for the latest status. Cancel plan Cancels the plan with Amazon. Mark as sent Tells RemBase the boxes left our building"}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "What you should see", "anchor": "what-you-should-see", "text": "After a button press, Inbound Pending shows a message, then clears. Inbound Result then says what happened and what to do next. After Confirm placement , the two box label files appear under Label Files . After Confirm freight (truck shipments), the pallet labels and the bill of lading appear too."}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "Products with two Amazon SKUs", "anchor": "products-with-two-amazon-skus", "text": "Some products have two Amazon SKUs: the original and a -stickered or -barcode version. RemBase treats both as the same product. The stock is counted on the original product. Becca chooses the one SKU to ship under. In the sku-map , she ticks Ship as on that SKU. If a product has two active SKUs and not exactly one is ticked, the shipment stops. Inbound Result says NOT DONE and asks Becca to tick Ship as . Nothing is sent to Amazon until this is fixed."}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Pressing a button twice because nothing seems to happen. Wait for Inbound Pending to clear. Using old labels. Always print from the shipment you are packing. Wrong label size. Use 4x6 for the thermal printer and 6-up for normal paper. Confirming without checking the price. Confirm placement and Confirm freight cost money. Practicing on this page. These buttons are real. There is no TEST shipment. Two Amazon SKUs with no Ship as tick. The shipment stops until Becca ticks Ship as on one SKU."}, {"page": "home.html", "chapter": "Home", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "Home shows how the business is doing: sales, stock, POs and Amazon shipments. It is in the menu under Home . Who uses it: Adam and Becca can open it for now. If you need access, ask Adam. This chapter covers five parts: Reports , Today so far , FBA storage space , Aged FBA stock and Listings . These parts only show information. Nothing here changes stock or orders."}, {"page": "home.html", "chapter": "Home", "section": "Reports", "anchor": "reports", "text": "Task: open a report Click Home in the menu. Click Reports . Menu with Home and Reports marked The top list is Newest file of each report . It has two groups: All brands – one file for all brands. One brand – one file for each brand. Find the report. Click its Drive Link . The file opens in Google Drive. Sign in to Google with your work account first. Newest file of each report, with the groups, Drive Link and Status marked Status C – Status shows if the file is up to date. Status What it means OK The file is up to date. Late The next file is overdue. Stale The file is too old. If a report says"}, {"page": "home.html", "chapter": "Home", "section": "Today so far", "anchor": "today-so-far", "text": "Today so far is at the top of the Home page (menu: Home → Home ). Today so far with all amounts blacked out and the Note marked The first box, Today so far (as of the time shown below) , shows today’s Amazon sales. The day is the Pacific time day. It is not a full day, and it includes estimated lines. It updates every hour. Pending orders often have no price yet. That part is an estimate . D – Note says how much is estimated. The final number for the day comes the next morning, in the daily sales. Under it, Sales (Amazon.com) starts with Last full day sales ."}, {"page": "home.html", "chapter": "Home", "section": "FBA storage space", "anchor": "fba-storage-space", "text": "FBA storage space is on the Home page (menu: Home → Home ). It shows how much space we use at Amazon, this month and next month. FBA storage space table with every number blacked out and the Level and colour bar marked E – Level and F – the colour bar show how full our space is: Level Colour What it means OK green Under 85% of our limit. Watch yellow 85% of the limit or more. Over red 100% of the limit or more. Our estimate counts our stock the same way Amazon does. It is usually a little higher than Amazon’s number (about 1–3%). The Level uses Amazon’s number while that number is less than a "}, {"page": "home.html", "chapter": "Home", "section": "Aged FBA stock", "anchor": "aged-fba-stock", "text": "Aged FBA stock (181+ days) is on the Home page (menu: Home → Home ). Aged FBA stock: the number of aged units and the list by brand, with every amount and ASIN blacked out K – Aged 181+ days (units): all our units at Amazon that are 181 days old or more. The list shows the same stock by brand. Each line shows its units and M – Est. Surcharge : Amazon’s estimate of the aged-stock fee. The bottom line shows the totals. L – Snapshot Date: the day Amazon counted the ages. It is usually a few days before today. N – Recommended Action and the sale price come from Amazon. Blank means Amazon gave none"}, {"page": "home.html", "chapter": "Home", "section": "Listings", "anchor": "listings", "text": "Listings shows problems with our Amazon listings (menu: Home → Listings ). Discontinued items are hidden. Listing alerts counters: Open P1, Open P2, Not buyable, Buy box problems Priority What it means P1 (urgent) The item sells 10 or more a month, and it is out of stock, not active, or its buy box is suppressed while it has stock. For our own brands, also when we lost the buy box. P2 Other real problems. P3 Low priority, for example discontinued items, other sellers’ brands, or alerts that keep going on and off. Not counted. G – Open P1 (urgent) and H – Open P2 count the alerts. I – Not buyab"}, {"page": "home.html", "chapter": "Home", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Opening a report while signed in to a personal Google account. Sign in with your work account first. Reading Today so far as the final number. It is an estimate until the next morning. Not telling Adam about Late or Stale. A Late or Stale report is out of date."}, {"page": "claims.html", "chapter": "Claims", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "Sometimes Amazon loses or damages our units. For example, Amazon does not receive every unit in a shipment, or a unit is damaged in an Amazon warehouse. Amazon pays us back, but only if we file a claim before the deadline. Claims → File Claims lists the claims we still need to file. RemBase finds them and prepares the text and the files for you. Who uses it: Karly files the claims every Monday. Adam can also open it. If you need access, ask Adam. Claims is real work now , not practice. These are real claims. You file each one in Amazon Seller Central . RemBase does not file it for you."}, {"page": "claims.html", "chapter": "Claims", "section": "The list", "anchor": "the-list", "text": "File Claims list with the shipment numbers and amounts blacked out The To file tab shows only claims that are not filed yet. Work from the top. A – Earliest Deadline: file before this date. B – Group Value (known): about how much Amazon should pay back. Blank means the cost is not known yet. Still file it. C – Case ID: empty until you file. Cost Unknown Lines: how many lines in the claim have no cost yet."}, {"page": "claims.html", "chapter": "Claims", "section": "The tabs", "anchor": "the-tabs", "text": "File Claims tabs: To file, Filed & closed, All records D – To file: claims you still need to file. This tab opens first. E – Filed & closed: claims that are filed, reimbursed, denied or closed. To find a claim you already filed, open this tab. F – All records: every claim (Airtable’s own tab)."}, {"page": "claims.html", "chapter": "Claims", "section": "Task: file a claim (every Monday)", "anchor": "task-file-a-claim-every-monday", "text": "Click Claims in the menu. Click File Claims . Start at the top of the list. Click a claim to open it. Read How To File . Its steps are different for each type of claim. Follow them. (For a Defective dispute , see below .) A claim with Case ID, Packet Text (blacked out) and How To File marked Click Open in Seller Central . Amazon’s page opens. Open in Seller Central, Search For and the evidence files, all documents blacked out In Amazon, search for the number in Search For . Copy the Packet Text and paste it into Amazon’s form. Look at Evidence Status . If Amazon asks for proof, attach the file"}, {"page": "claims.html", "chapter": "Claims", "section": "Defective dispute claims", "anchor": "defective-dispute-claims", "text": "Sometimes Amazon grades one of our returned or warehouse units as defective . Then Amazon does not pay us back. If we think the unit was damaged while Amazon handled it, we ask Amazon to check the grading again. These claims have the Group Type Defective dispute . There is one claim for each item each month. There is no minimum value. File every one. The Packet Text is ready to paste into the Amazon support case. To file one: Click Open in Seller Central on the claim. Amazon’s Get support page opens. Click Create new issue . Store: United States . Service: Selling on Amazon . Select My issue i"}, {"page": "claims.html", "chapter": "Claims", "section": "What you should see", "anchor": "what-you-should-see", "text": "After you type the Case ID , RemBase sets the claim to Filed and fills in Date Filed by itself. The claim leaves To file . You find it under Filed & closed . When the list is empty, you are done for the week."}, {"page": "claims.html", "chapter": "Claims", "section": "Fix a case number", "anchor": "fix-a-case-number", "text": "Wrong case number? Paste the right one into Case ID . The claim was not really filed? Delete the Case ID . The claim goes back to To file . Each case number belongs to one shipment. If Notes says DUPLICATE CASE ID , check which shipment the case is for."}, {"page": "claims.html", "chapter": "Claims", "section": "Claim status", "anchor": "claim-status", "text": "Status What it means Open Not filed yet. It is on the list. Filed Sent to Amazon. We wait for Amazon’s answer. Partly reimbursed Amazon paid back part of it. Reimbursed Amazon paid back all of it. Denied Amazon said no. Closed Nothing more to do."}, {"page": "claims.html", "chapter": "Claims", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Skipping a claim because the value is blank. Still file it. Forgetting the Case ID. Without it, RemBase thinks the claim is not filed. It stays on the list. Missing the deadline. After the Earliest Deadline , Amazon does not pay. Sending the wrong invoice. Check every CANDIDATE – check file before you attach it. Sending the highlighted copy. Amazon gets the original CANDIDATE file only."}, {"page": "other-pages.html", "chapter": "Other pages", "section": "Approvals", "anchor": "approvals", "text": "What it is for: some stock changes are big, for example a large count difference or a disposal. They wait here for a “yes” before they change the stock. Who uses it: Becca and Adam. What you see: Approvals → Ledger lists the waiting changes. Most days it is empty. Do not approve anything unless you are Becca or Adam."}, {"page": "other-pages.html", "chapter": "Other pages", "section": "Flags", "anchor": "flags", "text": "What it is for: a flag is a problem the system found. Examples: a part with no vendor, a count difference, a short Amazon shipment. Who uses it: Becca. Others may be assigned a flag. Sub-page What it shows My Open Flags Flags assigned to you. All Open Flags Every open flag. Open flags list To work on a flag: Click the flag. Read the Title and Note . Fix the cause in the right place, or ask the person for that area (see Who to ask ). When it is fixed, set Status to Resolved ."}, {"page": "other-pages.html", "chapter": "Other pages", "section": "Returns Grading", "anchor": "returns-grading", "text": "What it is for: Amazon sends products back to us (removal orders). We check each item and decide what to do with it. Who uses it: Sabith. Returns grading page, order ids hidden The list shows each returned product and how many we expect. After December 1, for each item: Count the items. Type the number in Received Qty (1). Choose a grade (2). Choose a Disposition (3): what we do with it. If you keep it, choose the Putaway Bin (4) and the Expiration Date . Before December 1, look only. Do not type on this page unless Becca asks."}, {"page": "other-pages.html", "chapter": "Other pages", "section": "Backorders", "anchor": "backorders", "text": "What it is for: PO lines that are still waiting for stock from the vendor. Who uses it: Becca. Everyone can look. Backordered PO lines, costs hidden This page is read-only. Click a line to see its PO."}, {"page": "other-pages.html", "chapter": "Other pages", "section": "CC Orders", "anchor": "cc-orders", "text": "What it is for: orders that Clear Conscience sends us for their customers. We pack and ship them. Who uses it: Sabith and Becca. CC Orders list, customer data hidden Before December 1, look only. Real CC orders are still handled the old way."}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Do not press", "anchor": "", "text": "Do not press any button on this page. These buttons email vendors, move real stock or delete records. If you think one is needed, ask Adam first ."}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Email PO", "anchor": "email-po", "text": "Email PO button marked do not press It emails the PO to the vendor."}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Email Staged POs and Delete Staged POs", "anchor": "email-staged-pos-and-delete-staged-pos", "text": "Email and delete staged POs buttons marked do not press They are at the bottom of the Purchase Orders list. They email or delete every staged PO at once."}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Production buttons", "anchor": "production-buttons", "text": "Finish Run on a real run – moves stock and adds units to the next Amazon shipment. (On your own practice run it is OK.) Reverse Run – undoes a finished run. See Production Run ."}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Planning buttons (Becca only)", "anchor": "planning-buttons-becca-only", "text": "Commit PO Planning and Clear PO Planning Selections Commit Run Planning and Clear Run Planning"}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Anything else", "anchor": "anything-else", "text": "Delete on any record. Create “…” in a part list. It makes a new part that planning leaves out. Ask Becca to add the part. New Part – Becca or Adam only. See Inventory . Add found item in a count. When in doubt: stop and ask ."}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Real buttons: be careful (Amazon shipments)", "anchor": "real-buttons-be-careful-amazon-shipments", "text": "The Amazon buttons on FBA Shipment → Next shipment are not on the do-not-press list. Anyone on the team may press them for a real shipment. They are real, not practice: The shipment buttons in the … menu Create plan , Refresh options , Re-check , Get prices again , Cancel plan , Mark as sent Confirm placement and Confirm freight cost money. Check the price first. Press once , then wait until Inbound Pending is empty. See FBA Shipment for what each button does."}, {"page": "glossary.html", "chapter": "Glossary", "section": "Glossary", "anchor": "", "text": "Word Meaning Bin A place on a shelf where stock is kept. Each bin has a name, like 01-A3. Lot One group of the same part with the same expiration date in the same bin. Expiration date The “use by” date on the box. FEFO “First expired, first out”. Use the stock that expires first. RemBase picks lots this way. Ledger The list of every stock move: receipts, runs, counts, shipments. On hand How many we have now. PO (purchase order) An order we send to a vendor. PO line One part on a PO, with its quantity and price. Vendor The company we buy from. Receipt The record that stock arrived. Outstanding "}, {"page": "who-to-ask.html", "chapter": "Who to ask", "section": "Who to ask", "anchor": "", "text": "Look in the handbook first. Then ask the person for that area. Area Ask Warehouse: bins, counts, builds, labels Chad Payments and receiving costs Vicky System problems and bugs (something in RemBase does not work) Adam Planning decisions and Becca’s approval buttons Becca Amazon claims Karly Any button on the Do not press list Adam , before you press Amazon shipments Anyone may press the shipment buttons. Not sure? Ask Adam first."}, {"page": "who-to-ask.html", "chapter": "Who to ask", "section": "When you ask, send", "anchor": "when-you-ask-send", "text": "The page name (for example: Receiving). The record name (for example: TEST-HB-1). What you clicked. What you expected to see. What you saw instead. A screenshot helps."}, {"page": "who-to-ask.html", "chapter": "Who to ask", "section": "Remember", "anchor": "remember", "text": "Until December 1, real work goes in Fishbowl . Practice only with TEST items. Not sure? Stop and ask. It is always OK to ask."}];
